  "goodToKnow": "Die Baumwolle is cotton, literally tree wool, as early European descriptions imagined sheep-like wool growing on trees. Labels show Baumwolle, Wolle (wool), Leinen (linen), Seide (silk) and Polyester. Germany's textile industry once centred on cotton spinning in Saxony and Westphalia. Today the Grüner Knopf (green button) label marks state-certified sustainable textiles. It has no plural."
